        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported left eye symptoms and related negatives"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Five days after the injury, the patient reports the left eye is much better, with a mild scratchy sensation and intermittent awareness of the eye, especially at the end of the work day. No significant pain, photophobia, or purulent discharge. Vision reported as back to normal. No flashes, floaters, curtain, or significant blur. No fevers or systemic symptoms."
      }
    },
